en to  add  but i'm not going to do that again just  as something  just just to clarify um but  they you know that it is important  actually that women are in those roles  when i was growing up  there were women in leadership roles  people like tessa jowl who went on to  become  a mentor of mine i cannot tell you how  much those women  matter in those leadership roles you  know people like diane abbott as well  really strong women who broke the mold  and and  and blazed a trail it really matters and  i'm absolutely determined that our  generation is not going to drop the ball  on this that we're going to keep seeing  progress  i remember during that labour leadership  contest uh you said at one point that  you'd quite like to see queen megan  i just wonder how you're feeling about  the cup some of the coverage  of meghan markle and prince harry you're  going to be watching the oprah winfrey  interview i feel like i absolutely  jinxed that i  should probably never have said it  because things have only got worse for  the royal family since  then and i have to say that i you know  my heart does go out to everybody  involved in this it's  difficult being in the public eye it's  particularly difficult when your family  is dragged into this and what i see when  i look at the royal family as a family  going through a very difficult time  all of it being played out in public  with maximum  publicity i think it would be far better  for them if they were able to  to deal with this privately behind the  scenes and and to be honest i think it  would be better for the country as well  they're having a very hard time but so  are hundreds of thousands of families  in this country at the moment because of  covid i think that they're the families  that we ought to be focusing on  okay lisa and andy thank you so much for  being on the program thank you  thank you now  it's been a very busy week but few  stories were more significant than  nicolas sturgeon giving evidence to the  inq